# AutoBuild-H5000M-Openwrt — repository hygiene.
#
# What this repo tracks is deliberately narrow: the scripts, config seeds,
# patches and CI that BUILD the firmware.  Nothing that a build produces or
# downloads belongs here, because the GitHub Action re-creates all of it from
# scratch and a committed copy would silently shadow the real thing.
#
# Tracked: README.md, LICENSE, .gitignore, .gitattributes, feeds.conf.default,
# .github/workflows/build.yml, configs/*, patches/*, mt76-patches/*,
# local-packages/*, scripts/*.sh  — 18 files.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The OpenWrt source tree. ~70 GB after a full build (source + toolchain +
# build_dir + bin), cloned at run time by scripts/local-build.sh into openwrt/
# (or into $SOURCE_DIR).  Never commit it.
#
# Builds normally happen in GitHub Actions, so this should not have to exist
# locally at all.  On btrfs with snapper, deleting the tree does not free the
# space until the snapshots that captured it are deleted as well.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
openwrt/
openwrt-*/
SOURCE_DIR/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Feed checkouts.  Installed by `scripts/feeds install` inside the source tree
# above; listed separately so an out-of-tree feeds/ checkout is covered too.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
feeds/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output.  artifacts/ is what scripts/local-build.sh publishes (firmware,
# manifest, apk repository, BUILD-INFO.txt); artifacts-coverage/ is what
# coverage-test.sh writes.  Both are reproducible from tracked sources.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
artifacts/
artifacts-*/
source.tar.gz

# The kernel ABI this build produced, written by build.yml so the NEXT pinned
# run can name the right apk-repo/<abi>/ directory before it compiles anything.
# A build output, not a source file: it changes every time a pin advances, and
# committing it would make the image's package source depend on what someone
# happened to commit rather than on what was actually built.
kernel-abi.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Packages cloned at build time: the three FAN789 board plugins, the Argon
# theme, the optional proxy stack and ddimension/wwand.  They are fetched into
# package/ (or $SOURCE_DIR/package/) on every run, so they must not be tracked —
# a stale committed copy would hide a clone failure instead of surfacing it.
# local-packages/ is NOT matched by this: that one is ours and IS tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
package/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Upstream pin bookkeeping, written by prepare_source.  Derived, not source.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.upstream-revision
.upstream-describe

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs and scratch.  Per-profile coverage logs land in the repo root.
#
# logs/ is the per-package build output OpenWrt writes when BUILD_LOG is on
# (scripts/local-build.sh passes it to make): logs/<package>/<step>.txt and
# logs/<subdir>/error.txt naming whatever failed.  Reproducible, and CI uploads
# it as an artifact when a build fails.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
build.log
logs/
coverage-*.log
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Migration-time reference checkouts (see README 九、迁移参考).  ~23 MB of
# other people's trees, kept locally for comparison only.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
refs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / OS / agent metadata.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.claude/
.agents/
.vscode/
.idea/
skills-lock.json
.toolchain-cache/
.buildcache/

# Signing keys must never be committed.  The CI installs one from a repository
# secret; a local build generates its own.
*.pem
private-key.pem
public-key.pem
.signing/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tool binaries that must never be committed.
#
# Scorecard's Binary-Artifacts check (a High-severity alert) caught a 5.1 MB
# `actionlint` binary in this repository: it had been downloaded to the working
# tree to run the workflow audit and was then swept in by `git add -A`.  A
# committed binary is an unreviewable blob — no diff, no provenance, and it
# bypasses the "this repo is pure source" property the project depends on.
#
# Tools are fetched by checks.yml / pre-commit from their pinned releases.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
actionlint
shfmt
shellcheck
zizmor
/tool-*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node dependencies.
#
# `npm ci` in the commitlint CI gate materialises this tree from
# package-lock.json; it is build output, never source.  Committing it once put
# 2240 files (291k lines) into a single commit — the lockfile is the artefact
# that belongs in the repository, and it is what pins integrity.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
